---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "CBD (Cannabidiol)"
letter: "C"
anchor: "cbd"
category: "cannabinoids"
---

The second most abundant cannabinoid in cannabis and the primary cannabinoid in hemp. CBD is non-intoxicating — it doesn't produce a high. It interacts with the endocannabinoid system through multiple pathways and has a growing research base for anxiety, epilepsy, and pain. The FDA has approved one CBD medication (Epidiolex) for severe epilepsy. CBD may also modify the THC experience; some studies suggest it softens THC's anxiety-inducing effects, while others found no difference.
